cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "dcrest: a differentiable implementation of the CREST rainfall-runoff model, with dCREST-CAMELS parameter sets"
message: "If you use this software or the parameter sets, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "HyDROS Lab, University of Oklahoma"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Skyan1002/dCREST"
version: "1.0.0"
keywords:
  - hydrology
  - rainfall-runoff
  - CREST
  - EF5
  - differentiable modelling
  - CAMELS
  - PyTorch
abstract: >-
  A differentiable, GPU-parallel PyTorch implementation of CREST (Coupled
  Routing and Excess Storage), the hydrologic core of the EF5 operational
  forecasting system. Discharge is differentiable with respect to both the
  parameters and the meteorological forcing, so parameters can be calibrated by
  gradient descent across thousands of catchments simultaneously and the model
  can be inverted for its input. Ships with dCREST-CAMELS, calibrated parameter
  sets for 665 CAMELS-US catchments produced under the community benchmark
  protocol.
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Wang
        given-names: Jiahu
    title: "The coupled routing and excess storage (CREST) distributed hydrological model"
    journal: "Hydrological Sciences Journal"
    volume: 56
    start: 84
    end: 98
    year: 2011
